 "Parental control questions": "index.html <span>",
 "How do I lock my child's iPhone remotely?": "index.html <span>",
 "Install Blok on your iPhone and your child's, and pair them with a code. Then tap LOCK in the app on your phone and the apps you chose are blocked on your child's phone. You can lock until further notice, for a set time, or with schedules.": "index.html <span>",
 "How quickly does the lock take effect?": "index.html <span>",
 "The lock is sent to your child's phone right away, but how fast it arrives depends on the phone's connection and iOS. If the phone is offline, the lock applies when it's back, and the app keeps retrying until the phone has answered. An app that's already open is locked the next time your child switches apps or unlocks the screen. Your phone shows when your child's phone has confirmed the lock.": "index.html <span>",
 "How is Blok different from Apple's Screen Time?": "index.html <span>",
 "Blok is built on Screen Time, but turns it into one tap from your own phone: lock now, timed locks and schedules, with a clear button that shows whether your child's phone is locked.": "index.html <span>",
 "What does my child need?": "index.html <span>",
 "An iPhone with iOS 16 or later and Blok installed. Your child needs no account of their own. You approve Screen Time on your child's phone once while pairing.": "index.html <span>",
 "Can my child remove the lock?": "index.html <span>",
 "Settings are protected by your PIN and iOS enforces the lock, so it holds even if the app is closed or the phone restarts. The only way around it is a factory reset of the phone, which no parental control can prevent.": "index.html <span>",
 "Can my child still make calls?": "index.html <span>",
 "Yes. You choose which apps are locked, so Phone and Messages can stay open. Emergency calls always work.": "index.html <span>",
 "Does Blok monitor what my child does?": "index.html <span>",
 "No. Blok reads no messages, tracks no location and doesn't collect which apps your child uses. The choice of apps to lock stays on your child's phone.": "index.html <span>",
 "Can I block TikTok, YouTube, Snapchat or games?": "index.html <span>",
 "Yes. When you pair the phones, you choose which apps on your child's iPhone get locked, for example TikTok, YouTube, Snapchat, Instagram, Roblox or other games. Phone, Messages and any other apps you want open keep working.": "index.html <span>",
 "How much does Blok cost?": "index.html <span>",
 "Blok has a subscription, Blok Plus, and the price for your country is shown in the App Store. Unlocking your child's phone always works, even without a subscription. Blok has no ads.": "index.html <span>",
 "Are there other apps called Blok?": "index.html <span>",
 "Yes, the name is common. This app is called Blok: Parental Control and is made for families: a parent locks the apps on their child's iPhone from their own iPhone. It isn't an app for limiting your own screen time. Look for the icon: a white padlock on a blue circle.": "index.html <span>",
 "Does Blok work on Android?": "index.html <span>",
 "Not yet. Blok is built for iPhone, for both you and your child.": "index.html <span>",
 "Give your child a break from the phone.": "index.html <span>",
 "Privacy Policy": "index.html <span>",
 "Terms of Use": "index.html <span>",
 "Privacy Policy – Blok: Parental Control": "privacy.html <title>",
 "Privacy policy for Blok, parental control for iPhone. What data we process, why, where it is stored (EU) and how to delete it.": "privacy.html <meta description>",
 "This page is a translation for your convenience. If it differs from the <a href=\"../en/privacy.html\">English version</a>, the English version applies.": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Last updated 14 October 2026": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Blok locks your child's phone, and that's it. We only collect what the lock needs to work, and never what your child does on the phone.": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Who we are": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Blok is developed and run by the app's developer, who is the data controller under the GDPR. Contact: <a class=\"email\" href=\"mailto:eliastestdev@gmail.com\">eliastestdev@gmail.com</a>.": "privacy.html <span>",
 "What Blok does": "privacy.html <span>",
 "A parent uses Blok on their own iPhone to lock and unlock their child's iPhone. The lock is enforced by Apple's Screen Time technology on the child's phone.": "privacy.html <span>",
 "What we process and why": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Data": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Why": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Kept": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Parent sign-in identifier (Sign in with Apple; the email is only an Apple relay address if you chose to hide it)": "privacy.html <span>",
 "To know which parent may control which phone": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Until you delete the account": "privacy.html <span>",
 "The child's phone: a name you choose, iPhone model, iOS version, pairing time, last sync and whether Screen Time is approved": "privacy.html <span>",
 "To show the phone in your app and send the lock to the right phone": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Until you remove the phone or delete the account": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Lock settings (locked/unlocked, timer, schedules, time zone), the phone's actual state and the number of apps set to lock": "privacy.html <span>",
 "To enforce and show the lock": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Parent PIN recovery code": "privacy.html <span>",
 "So you can get back in if you forget the PIN. Only the parent can read it.": "privacy.html <span>",
 "The child's phone push token and notification setting": "privacy.html <span>",
 "To tell the phone the lock has changed": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Until you remove the phone": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Subscription status": "privacy.html <span>",
 "To know whether the subscription is active": "privacy.html <span>",
 "As long as the subscription exists": "privacy.html <span>",
 "What we never collect": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Which apps are on the child's phone or which apps you chose to lock (that choice stays on the child's phone; only the number is reported), what the child does on the phone, location, messages, contacts or any other content. The app contains no analytics or advertising tools.": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Processors": "privacy.html <span>",
 "<strong>Google Firebase</strong> (sign-in, database, server functions, push). Data is stored in the EU: the database in Europe (eur3), the server functions in Belgium (europe-west1).": "privacy.html <span>",
 "<strong>RevenueCat</strong> (subscription status, an anonymous user id only).": "privacy.html <span>",
 "<strong>Apple</strong> (Sign in with Apple, push and purchases).": "privacy.html <span>",
 "They process the data only on our instructions and under their data-processing terms.": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Legal basis and children": "privacy.html <span>",
 "We process the data to perform the contract with the parent (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR). Data from the child's phone is processed on the parent's instruction as the holder of parental responsibility. The child never creates an account and is never asked for personal data; the phone is identified by an anonymous technical id.": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Security": "privacy.html <span>",
 "All traffic is encrypted. The child phone's credential is stored in the iOS Keychain. Each phone can only read its own records, and every change goes through server functions.": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Your rights": "privacy.html <span>",
 "You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability and to object. Deleting your account in the app, or emailing us, removes all the data above within 30 days. You can also complain to the Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection (IMY), <a href=\"https://www.imy.se\">imy.se</a>.": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Email us": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Changes": "privacy.html <span>",
 "If we change this policy, we update this page and the date at the top.": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Home": "privacy.html <span>",
 "Support – Blok: Parental Control": "support.html <title>",
 "Help with Blok: the lock doesn't take effect, forgotten parent PIN, re-pairing a phone, subscription and deleting your account. Email us.": "support.html <meta description>",
 "Support": "support.html <span>",
 "Something not working, or a question? Email us and we'll answer as soon as we can, usually within a couple of working days.": "support.html <span>",
 "Contact us": "support.html <span>",
 "It helps to tell us which iPhone and iOS version it is, and whether it's your phone or your child's.": "support.html <span>",
 "Email support": "support.html <span>",
 "The lock doesn't take effect": "support.html <span>",
 "Check that your child's phone is online. The lock arrives once it's connected again.": "support.html <span>",
 "An app that's already open is locked the next time your child switches apps or unlocks the screen.": "support.html <span>",
 "Open Blok on your child's phone and check that you've picked the apps to lock. No apps picked means nothing is locked.": "support.html <span>",
 "Screen Time must be approved on your child's phone. Open Blok there; the app tells you if anything is missing.": "support.html <span>",
 "I forgot the parent PIN": "support.html <span>",
 "Open Blok on your phone, go to Settings and tap your child's phone. The recovery code is there.": "support.html <span>",
 "Changing or re-pairing a phone": "support.html <span>",
 "On your phone: Settings, tap your child's phone and choose \"New pairing code\". Enter the code in Blok on your child's phone.": "support.html <span>",
 "Subscription": "support.html <span>",
 "Cancel: Settings on your iPhone, tap your name, then Subscriptions.": "support.html <span>",
 "New phone? Tap \"Restore purchases\" in Blok.": "support.html <span>",
 "Refunds are handled by Apple: <a href=\"https://reportaproblem.apple.com\">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.": "support.html <span>",
 "Unlocking always works, even without a subscription.": "support.html <span>",
